        "original_id": "d843837c-9ddf-5671-90ea-d1e665cc3cf9",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Old Fashioned, gin and tonic, Henry Bain sauce\n- Organizations: Pendennis Club\n- Places: Louisville, Kentucky\n- Concepts: cocktails, condiments\n\nFacts:\n- Sometime in the 1880s, the Pendennis Club was the birthplace by name, not invention, of the Old Fashioned.\n- The Old Fashioned was possibly the first mixed drink to be called a cocktail.\n- The Old Fashioned is a cocktail made by muddling sugar with bitters, then adding alcohol such as whiskey or brandy and a twist of citrus rind.\n- A gin and tonic is a highball cocktail made with gin and tonic water poured over ice.\n- A gin and tonic is usually garnished with a slice or wedge of lime.\n- Henry Bain sauce is a condiment for meats that was first served at the Pendennis Club in Louisville, Kentucky.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
